 ## Architecture
 
@@ -23,4 +23,17 @@ Resolve the immutable source revision before rendering. The cache key includes c
 
 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The cache uses a **2Q eviction policy** with two queues:
+
+- **Am queue (A1)**: First-use entries. New entries are inserted at the head of A1. On each cache hit in A1, the entry is promoted to the head of the Am queue. When A1 exceeds its size limit, the tail entry is evicted.
+- **Am queue (A2)**: Reused entries. Entries promoted from A1 on their second access enter at the head of Am. On each cache hit in Am, the entry is moved to the head of Am. When Am exceeds its size limit, the tail entry is evicted.
+
+The total cache size (A1 + Am) must not exceed 12 GiB. The A1 size limit is set to 25% of the total cache budget (3 GiB); the Am limit is the remainder (9 GiB). Both limits are enforced in bytes of cached JPEG data.
+
+Eviction order: when admitting a new entry would exceed the total budget, evict from A1 tail first until A1 is within its limit, then evict from Am tail. This ensures one-use entries from sequential scans are evicted before promoted comparison sheets.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|------------------------|-----------|
+| 2Q eviction policy with 25%/75% A1/Am split | LRU; Frequency-based with aging | 2Q protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets during long sequential screenings. LRU evicts comparison sheets during scans. Frequency-based adds counter maintenance and ages slowly on project switches. The 25% A1 split reserves space for the working set while limiting scan pollution. All policies keep the external interface, queue concurrency, and disk budget unchanged. See [decision doc](../decisions/001-2q-eviction-policy.md). |
