 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a preview is accessed for the first time and admitted to the cache, the system SHALL place it in the A1 queue at the head position.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a preview in the A1 queue is accessed again, the system SHALL promote it to the head of the Am queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a preview in the Am queue is accessed, the system SHALL move it to the head of the Am queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When the A1 queue exceeds 3 GiB, the system SHALL evict entries from the tail of A1 until it is within the limit.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When the Am queue exceeds 9 GiB, the system SHALL evict entries from the tail of Am until it is within the limit.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When admitting a new preview would exceed the total 12 GiB budget, the system SHALL evict from A1 tail first, then from Am tail, until the total is within budget.
